From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hi846: Allow every analogue gain step

The analogue gain control took steps of 8 codes, and the control core
rounds a value to the nearest step: with gain = 1 + code / 16 only every
0.5x reached the sensor. An AGC that models the gain in steps of 1/16, as
the register allows, then saw the gains it asked for between 1.5x and 2x
land on two values 33% apart, and hunted between them: the whole frame
pumped about once a second.

The register takes the codes between: measured on the Huawei MateBook E
Go with the front camera under a white paper and a fixed exposure, each
of the codes 8 to 16, written directly over I2C, gives 1 + code / 16
within 0.3%. Let the control take a step of 1.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
index 704892eaa..5117be0bb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@
 #define HI846_REG_ANALOG_GAIN		0x0077
 #define HI846_ANAL_GAIN_MIN		0
 #define HI846_ANAL_GAIN_MAX		240
-#define HI846_ANAL_GAIN_STEP		8
+#define HI846_ANAL_GAIN_STEP		1
 
 /* Digital gain controls from sensor */
 #define HI846_REG_MWB_GR_GAIN_H		0x0078
